WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.418
Water is connected across whole landscapes.

2
00:00:03.538 --> 00:00:08.458
In this tutorial, you will learn how to use
the map widgets to filter stations,

3
00:00:08.578 --> 00:00:13.114
search by place or coordinates, and build
custom monitoring areas.

4
00:00:13.917 --> 00:00:16.557
This is the MyWell map workspace.

5
00:00:16.677 --> 00:00:23.445
Floating filter chips across the top let you explore and refine
the monitoring network without covering your view of the map.

6
00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:30.754
The Scope chip switches between My stations — the
wells and rain gauges you manage — and All stations,

7
00:00:30.874 --> 00:00:35.338
which reveals every shared public monitoring
station across the region.

8
00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:43.926
The Type filter lets you focus on specific water sources:
open wells, borewells, rain gauges, check dams,

9
00:00:44.046 --> 00:00:46.542
rivers, and storage tanks.

10
00:00:46.662 --> 00:00:49.806
Each source type has a unique icon and colour.

11
00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:56.281
The Distance widget filters stations within a set
radius from your location or a chosen point.

12
00:00:56.401 --> 00:01:03.313
Pick a quick shortcut or slide to see all stations
within two, five, ten, or twenty kilometres.

13
00:01:04.117 --> 00:01:10.045
The search bar lets you find stations by name
or code, locate villages and places,

14
00:01:10.165 --> 00:01:15.061
or jump directly to exact GPS latitude and
longitude coordinates.

15
00:01:15.883 --> 00:01:19.579
Under Actions, select Create monitoring area.

16
00:01:19.699 --> 00:01:24.859
This arms the area tool so you can group
neighbouring stations into a named cluster —

17
00:01:24.979 --> 00:01:29.515
such as a village boundary, micro-catchment,
or local network.

18
00:01:30.317 --> 00:01:36.005
Once you select your stations or apply a
radius, name your monitoring area and save it.

19
00:01:36.125 --> 00:01:39.125
Your area is stored under your account,

20
00:01:39.245 --> 00:01:43.949
and you can re-open it any time to view
combined trends and statistics.

21
00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:46.694
That is the whole page.

22
00:01:46.814 --> 00:01:51.470
You can replay this tutorial any time from the
Learning page inside the app.

23
00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:54.254
Thanks for helping look after our water.
